* Task 27 fixture: variable use-site scanner (extractVariableRefs)
* Exercises variable identifier captures in statement bodies:
* - Basic captures: scalar, group-qualified fields, REDEFINE sub-fields, arrays
* - Subscript stripping: array subscripts are stripped, index vars are separate refs
* - Comment/string exclusion: variables in comments and string literals are NOT captured
* - System var exclusion: *-system vars like *DATE are NOT captured
* - Dynamic (`&`) exclusion: & sigils are excluded (modeled gap)

DEFINE DATA
LOCAL
  1 #CUSTOMER-NAME (A40)
  1 #COUNTER (N5)
  1 #GROUP
    2 #FIELD-1 (A20)
    2 #FIELD-2 (N8)
  1 #REDEF-FIELD (A30)
    2 #SUB-FIELD-1 REDEFINE #REDEF-FIELD (N5)
    2 #SUB-FIELD-2 REDEFINE #REDEF-FIELD (A10)
  1 #TABLE (A10/1:5)
  1 #INDEX (N2)
END-DEFINE

* Line with variable uses in MOVE
MOVE #CUSTOMER-NAME TO #COUNTER
MOVE 100 TO #GROUP.#FIELD-1

* Variable in IF condition
IF #COUNTER > 0
  COMPUTE #FIELD-2 = #COUNTER + 1
END-IF

* Variable in array subscript — the index #INDEX is its own ref
MOVE #TABLE(#INDEX) TO #CUSTOMER-NAME

* Variable in WRITE
WRITE #SUB-FIELD-1 #SUB-FIELD-2

* Variable in CALLNAT argument
CALLNAT 'SUB1' #REDEF-FIELD #COUNTER

* Comment with false positives (should NOT be captured)
* This is a comment with #FIELD inside it

* String literal with false positive (should NOT be captured)
MOVE '#CUSTOMER-NAME' TO #COUNTER

* System variable (should NOT be captured)
MOVE *DATE TO #COUNTER

* Dynamic substitution (should NOT be captured or flagged separately)
CALLNAT #CALLNAT-NAME #COUNTER

END
